  "summary": "Payload vulnerable to API key disclosure through ordinary document reads",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nUsers with read access to other user documents could access their active API keys. An exposed key grants the target account’s permissions until rotated or disabled.\n\nYou are affected if:\n\n- An authentication collection enables `useAPIKey`.\n- Users have read access to other user documents containing active API keys.\n\n### Patches\n\nUsers should upgrade payload packages to `>= 3.90.0` or `>= 4.0.0-canary.34`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDisable `useAPIKey` or restrict users to reading only their own authentication document. Rotate any API key that may have been exposed.",
